lox add locksql: one database, applied at once (Ctrl-C before the review: nothing is kept)

Engine: postgres, mysql, mariadb or sqlite (required) [postgres]: mariadb
Host (required) [host.docker.internal]: db.example.com
Port (required) [3306]: 
User (optional: empty = the console asks for it at start with the password): shop
Database (optional: empty = the server's default database): orders
Production? (tickets flagged production; the profile name is typed at the console's start) [y/N] y
Credentials: ask (typed, masked, at the console's start) or vault (required) [ask]: vault
Vault path (required) [database/creds/db]: 
Vault address, such as https://vault.example.com:8200 (required): https://vault.example.com:8200
Vault namespace (optional: empty = the root namespace): 
Vault CA file (optional: empty = the system's CA certificates): 
Name (required) [db]: orders
